<!--
  MachineBlocks — concept documentation

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept.GeometryConcepts
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:concept="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.concept"
  xmlns:mbcore="com.machineblocks.bml.core">

  <name>GeometryConcepts</name>
  <type>concept:GeometryConcepts</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>A guide to MachineBlocks shape modification concepts</is>

  <documentation>
    Core geometry parameters modify the block shape inside the bounding box defined by size:

    size — integer grid extent; the spatial contract of the block.
    sizeMod — semantic per-side modification that keeps the brick structurally intact.
    slope — height change per side; positive slopes the top, negative creates inverted bottom
      slopes. Does not change footprint.
    bevel — footprint change by shifting top corners in XY; produces wedge shapes. Does not change
      height. Wedges are not a separate primitive — they emerge from bevel.
    crop — hard cut or extension; does not preserve grid compatibility, walls, or structural
      features; does not change bounding box or positioning; corner rounding applies after crop.
    Prefer sizeMod over crop when the brick should remain structurally intact.

    Cutouts are an array of settings arrays. Each inner array defines one cut volume using geometry
    and size parameters. The cutout is boolean-subtracted from the body. Surface-only and
    render-only parameters are ignored in a cutout context.

    Parameter names, types, and defaults are defined on NativeBlock — do not treat external YAML or
    Markdown tables as authoritative.
  </documentation>

  <references>
    <see type="concept:TransformationConcepts" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — direction, alignment, rotation, and transform order.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:NativeBlock" relation="Defines">
      SSOT for size, sizeMod, slope, bevel, crop, cutouts, and related properties.
    </see>
    <see type="concept:DecisionFramework" relation="SeeAlso">
      When slope and bevel should not share a single native call.
    </see>
  </references>

</block>
